* Dequeue :: Right. One read and an index update.
* Reading the i-th item of the queue, counting from the front :: Right. It's `slots[(front + i) % cap]`: one calculation.
* Checking whether it's full :: Right. `size == cap`.
- Listing every item in order :: That visits all of them: O(size).
- Making room for more items than `cap` :: The array has a fixed size. Growing it means copying every item: O(n).
hint: Which ones touch a fixed number of slots?
hint: Four of them are O(1).
